{
  "dom_id": "questionContainer",
  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14196632/assets/a61a6232b2041bab3d455a7d765311ddfae25f674f8dbbf79696d2137355b159.png)\n\nThe Venn diagram shown above represents two events $A$ and $B$ and the number of outcomes in each region of the sample space.\n\nGiven that every outcome is equally likely, find $P({A}^{′}\\cup {B}^{′}).$",
  "worked_solution": "To calculate the probability of an event using a Venn diagram, we count the number of outcomes in the region that represents the event, and divide by the total number of outcomes of the sample space $S.$\n\nIn the Venn diagram, ${A}^{′}\\cup {B}^{′}$ is represented by the area outside the circle $B$ or outside the circle $A$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14196632/assets/6a3bb7b671e45aeb15d3239cae6fcedb7c36e52b15141d66b23e65066ab37edc.png)\n\nWe count up the outcomes:\n\n- The number of outcomes in ${A}^{′}\\cup {B}^{′}$ is \n\n$$\n2+5+1=8\n$$\n\n- The total number of outcomes in $S$ is\n\n$$\n2+9+5+1=17.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP({A}^{′}\\cup {B}^{′})=\\frac{8}{17}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
